# Build-context allowlist for `docker build -f build/docker/Dockerfile .`
# (Phase 32, Unit 32.10). Docker reads the .dockerignore at the build-context
# root; the gateway image is built with the repository root as context, so this
# file lives here.
#
# Everything is excluded by default and only what `go build ./cmd/qsdev` needs
# is re-included. A denylist missed local, gitignored material that sits in
# the checkout: the ~1 GB .go/ module cache, bin/, the root qsdev binary,
# mcp.db, and .qsdev/ (which holds mcp-secrets.env). The Dockerfile does
# `COPY . .`, so anything in the context lands in a builder layer that
# --cache-to can export.
#
# The Go workspace (go.work, which `use`s ../gdev) stays out: the build uses
# GOWORK=off + -mod=vendor.
*

!go.mod
!go.sum
!vendor/
!addons/
!cmd/
!instance/
!internal/
# nix/ holds the derivations the binary embeds (nix/embed.go).
!nix/
!pkg/
!rules/

# Secret material must never enter the context, even inside the re-included
# trees above (operators place ./tls/server.key etc. next to the sources).
**/.qsdev/
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.env
**/*.key
**/*.pem
**/*.crt
**/tls/

# Test scratch that may appear inside the re-included trees.
**/*.tmp
